
# The sync-managed block above ignores `lib` (top-level symlink) but the
# pattern also matches src/lib/ and harness/lib/. Un-ignore both trees.
!src/lib
!src/lib/**
!scripts/lib
!scripts/lib/**
!harness
!harness/**

# Bassclef runtime artifacts (per-machine, not content)
.claude/LAST_SAVE
.claude/SESSION_LOCK
.claude/CHECKPOINT.md
.claude/settings.local.json
state/markers/verify/

# Node.js / npm build artifacts (WU-1)
node_modules/
dist/
*.tgz
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.local

# Substrate bundle — populated by prepublishOnly at publish time; never committed.
# Per ADR-007 D1 (bundle path lock at substrate/<path>).
substrate/

# Bassclef SDLC + runtime marker directories (per-session, not content)
docs/sdlc-traces/
state/markers/verify/
state/markers/hook-heartbeat/
state/markers/turn-counter/
state/markers/diagnose/
state/markers/session-timing/
state/markers/turn-grade/
state/markers/turn-prose-flags/
# cli#466 follow-on — same per-turn write cadence as turn-prose-flags above.
# Two Stop hooks rewrite these every turn (turn-prose-density-measure.sh,
# turn-prose-kiss-check.sh). Tracked, they were auto-committed and pushed
# per turn, restarting the 12-min lite-adopter smoke. Root cure upstream at
# bassclef-upstream#2366 (save-state.sh git add -u ignores its own pathspecs).
state/markers/turn-prose-density/
state/markers/turn-prose-appositive/
state/markers/turn-prose-surface/

# cli#169 — vitest test-run history (local-only per ADR-049; never committed).
# Vitest JSON reporter writes here on every `npm test`; `npm run test:report`
# aggregates via scripts/aggregate-test-runs.sh.
state/events/test-runs/

# Bassclef-sync managed symlinks — subdirectories the top block missed
# (session-reflection.d gets populated by user-scope sync too)
.claude/hooks/session-reflection.d/

# Un-ignore harness/ tree AFTER the sync-managed `lib` pattern above —
# rule order matters (later wins). The bare `lib` in the managed block
# would otherwise re-ignore harness/lib. Iteration i (2026-08-27) added.
!harness
!harness/**

# Un-ignore harness/ tree AFTER the sync-managed `lib` pattern above —
# rule order matters (later wins). The bare `lib` in the managed block
# would otherwise re-ignore harness/lib. Iteration i (2026-08-27) added.
!harness
!harness/**

# The sync-managed block above ignores a bare `lib` pattern that also
# matches src/lib/ and harness/lib/. Un-ignore those trees AFTER the
# managed block — later rules win in .gitignore.
!src/lib
!src/lib/**
!scripts/lib
!scripts/lib/**
!harness
!harness/**

# Substrate synced from bassclef into this repo at session start. These
# files belong to the operator's machine, not to the cli source tree.
# Only .claude/settings.json and .claude/bassclef-configs.jsonc are ours.
# Added 2026-09-17 after `git add -A` swept ~575 of them into a PR.
# One exception: .claude/skills/publish is OURS. It drives this repo's
# release gate and exists in neither public bassclef nor upstream, so the
# sync cannot put it back. Ignoring it left the skill on one machine, never
# in git, one `git clean -xdf` from gone. Per #511.
#
# The form matters. `.claude/skills/` excludes the directory and git will not
# descend into it, so a `!` negation underneath has no effect. Ignoring the
# CONTENTS instead leaves room for the exception, and `git add -A` still
# cannot sweep the synced copies.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/publish
.claude/rules/
.claude/agents/
.claude/luminaries/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/embeddings/
.claude/bassclef-orientation.md
.claude/*.bak.*
/lib/

# Vitest coverage output (cli#165)
coverage/
*.lcov

# docker-smoke local run output (bind-mount landing)
harness-out/

# Live-driver captures from scripts/smoke-drive-*.sh — local only
docs/smoke-captures/
# >>> bassclef-sync managed symlinks (do not edit) >>>
CLAUDE.md.bak.*
# <<< bassclef-sync managed symlinks <<<
